WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.347
Cut a whole into equal parts,
and every part is a fraction.

2
00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:12.886
Today you compare fractions, share
amounts, and write percentages.

3
00:00:13.386 --> 00:00:16.730
Here is one whole bar.
Cut it into 2 equal parts.

4
00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:21.455
Each part is a half. Now cut
the same bar into 4 equal parts.

5
00:00:21.675 --> 00:00:25.808
Each part is a quarter, and a
quarter is half the size of a half.

6
00:00:26.028 --> 00:00:30.532
Cut the bar into 8, and each
part is an eighth. Smaller again.

7
00:00:30.752 --> 00:00:34.886
The whole never changes, so more
parts always means smaller parts.

8
00:00:35.106 --> 00:00:38.542
So a bigger bottom number
does not mean a bigger piece.

9
00:00:39.042 --> 00:00:42.711
Three cakes are shared
fairly between four children.

10
00:00:42.931 --> 00:00:46.785
Cut every cake into quarters.
That gives twelve equal quarters.

11
00:00:47.005 --> 00:00:50.210
Now share the twelve
quarters out, one at a time.

12
00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:52.845
Each child gets three quarters of a cake.

13
00:00:53.065 --> 00:00:57.105
Three cakes divided by four
children: the cakes go on top.

14
00:00:57.605 --> 00:01:01.599
A unit fraction is an
instruction. Find one fifth of 20.

15
00:01:01.819 --> 00:01:05.952
The bottom number says how many
equal groups to make, so make five.

16
00:01:06.172 --> 00:01:09.841
Share the 20 counters out
fairly. Each group holds four.

17
00:01:10.061 --> 00:01:13.822
One group is the answer,
so one fifth of 20 is 4.

18
00:01:14.042 --> 00:01:18.454
It is not 5. The 5 told you how
many groups, not the answer.

19
00:01:18.954 --> 00:01:23.645
Two fractions can look different
and still be worth exactly the same.

20
00:01:23.865 --> 00:01:28.555
Here is one half of a bar, and here
are two quarters of the same bar.

21
00:01:28.775 --> 00:01:33.047
The shading ends in the same place,
so one half equals two quarters.

22
00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:37.447
Four eighths reaches there too.
All three are equivalent fractions.

23
00:01:37.947 --> 00:01:42.637
Per cent means out of a hundred.
Here are a hundred small squares.

24
00:01:42.857 --> 00:01:47.037
Shade 25 of them, and you have
shaded 25 per cent of the grid.

25
00:01:47.257 --> 00:01:51.204
You write it with the per
cent sign, like this: 25%.

26
00:01:51.424 --> 00:01:55.325
Those 25 shaded squares fill
one quarter of the whole grid.

27
00:01:55.545 --> 00:01:59.353
So one quarter and 25 per
cent are the very same amount.

28
00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:02.733
Which is bigger, three
quarters or five eighths?

29
00:02:02.953 --> 00:02:07.039
Give them the same bottom number
first. Cut every quarter in two.

30
00:02:07.259 --> 00:02:10.092
Three quarters is the same
amount as six eighths.

31
00:02:10.312 --> 00:02:14.260
Now only the top numbers
matter, and six beats five.

32
00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:17.173
So three quarters is
bigger than five eighths.

33
00:02:17.673 --> 00:02:21.621
More parts means smaller parts,
and a fraction is a division.

34
00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:25.416
To find a fraction of an amount,
share it into equal groups.

35
00:02:25.636 --> 00:02:29.723
Fractions can be worth the same,
and per cent means out of a hundred.

36
00:02:29.943 --> 00:02:34.262
Give two fractions the same bottom
number, and you can compare them.
